# Phase 11.1 – Minor Enhancements (Generate Report, Release Readiness & Settings)

## Objective

This phase focuses on minor usability improvements, exclusion handling enhancements, tooltip improvements, deployment readiness behavior refinements, and settings cleanup.

These changes are incremental improvements and **must not modify any existing working business logic**.

---

# Acceptance Criteria

## 1. Introduce User Exclusion Alongside System Exclusion

### Current Behavior

Components can currently be excluded only through the predefined iTrack exclusion configuration.

These exclusions are automatically ignored during report generation.

### Required Enhancement

Introduce two different exclusion types:

- System Excluded (configured through iTrack/team configuration)
- User Excluded (selected manually by the user from the Component Preview screen)

Both exclusion types must be stored independently.

Example:

- exclude (System)
- userExclude (User)

Do not merge both into one field.

---

## 2. Component Preview – User Exclude Option

While selecting components before Generate Report:

Users should be able to manually exclude any component.

This exclusion should be stored as:

- userExclude = true

System exclusions remain untouched.

---

## 3. Generate Report Must Respect User Exclusions

During Generate Report:

Current logic already skips:

- System Excluded components

Enhance the logic to also skip:

- User Excluded components

Both exclusion types must be ignored during:

- Commit Analysis
- Story Mapping
- Compliance Analysis
- Violation Detection
- Report Generation

No external calls should be performed for excluded components.

---

# Release Readiness Enhancements

## 4. Branch Cut Validation - Hide System Exclusions

Current behavior shows all components.

Required:

Do NOT display components excluded through iTrack/System configuration.

Those components are intentionally excluded.

Therefore they should not participate in Branch Cut Validation.

---

## 5. Branch Cut Validation - Show User Exclusions

Unlike system exclusions,

User Excluded components should still appear in Branch Cut Validation.

Reason:

Users excluded them manually.

Branch Cut validation should still indicate their status.

These components should remain visible but clearly marked as User Excluded.

---

