# Deployment Readiness Improvements

## 8. Force Refresh Should Work Only For Selected Environment

Current implementation:

Force Refresh All Environments

refreshes every environment.

This is not required.

Required:

Only refresh the currently selected environment.

Example:

Selected:

Test-3

Refresh should call ONLY:

Test-3

NOT:

- Test-4
- Stage-West
- Production-East
- Production-West

---

## 9. Hide Refresh Button Until Environment Selected

Current behavior:

Refresh button always visible.

Required:

If no environment selected:

Hide:

Force Refresh Deployment Readiness

After selecting an environment:

Display:

Force Refresh Deployment Readiness

---

## 10. Invalid Only Switch

Current behavior appears regardless of selection.

Required:

Invalid Only switch should become visible only after an environment is selected.

No environment

↓

No switch.

Environment selected

↓

Switch visible.

---

## 11. Deployment Validation Scope

Every deployment validation must execute only for:

Selected Environment

Never invoke APIs for all environments unless an explicit "Refresh All" feature is introduced in the future.

---

## 12. Backend API Optimization

Ensure deployment backend receives:

Selected Environment

↓

Namespace

↓

Deployment Validation

Only.

No unnecessary Kubernetes calls.

---

# Settings Page Enhancement

## 13. Replace Test-3/Test-4 Cookies

Current Settings page contains:

- Test-3 Cookie
- Test-4 Cookie

This is incorrect.

Actual infrastructure uses:

One Test Cookie

shared across all Test namespaces.

Replace:

- Test-3 Cookie
- Test-4 Cookie

with:

Test Kubernetes Cookie

This single cookie must be reused for:

- Test-1 (future)
- Test-2 (future)
- Test-3
- Test-4

---

## 14. Backend Cookie Mapping

Backend should also maintain:

Test Cookie

instead of

Test-3 Cookie

Test-4 Cookie

All Test namespace authentication should reuse the same cookie.

---

## 15. Preserve Existing Deployment Logic

Existing deployment status logic should remain unchanged.

Only improve:

- Environment selection
- Refresh behavior
- Cookie reuse
- UI visibility

No existing deployment validation should break.

---

# General Requirements

## 16. Backward Compatibility

All current working functionality must continue to work.

Do not modify existing report generation behavior other than adding User Exclusion support.

---

## 17. UI Consistency

Maintain the same design language already introduced across the application.

Do not introduce new styles.

Reuse:

- Existing badges
- Existing tooltip components
- Existing switches
- Existing status indicators

---

## 18. Testing Checklist

Before completing this phase, verify:

- System Excluded components hidden from Branch Cut Validation
- User Excluded components visible in Branch Cut Validation
- Generate Report ignores User Excluded components
- Generate Report ignores System Excluded components
- Team tooltip displays complete team list
- Story tooltip displays complete story list
- Force Refresh only refreshes selected environment
- Refresh button hidden until environment selected
- Invalid Only switch visible only after environment selection
- Settings page contains only one Test Kubernetes Cookie
- Backend reuses Test Cookie across all Test namespaces
- Existing functionality remains unaffected

